// Generated by scripts/seventyTwoAngels/assemble.ts from the OCR of
// Lazare Lenain, La Science Cabalistique (Amiens, 1823), which is public
// domain. The French is that scan repaired; the English is translated from
// the repaired French. Neither draws on any modern published translation.
// Everything Lenain's four tables make derivable — degrees, dates, hours,
// decade, planet, choir — lives in seventyTwoAngelsDerived.ts, not here.
// See plan 031.
[
  "1st genius, Vehuiah, והויה. His attribute is interpreted (God elevated and exalted above all things). He rules over the Hebrews. The name of God, according to this language, is called Jehovah. He governs the first ray of the Orient in the season of spring, that is to say the first five degrees of the sphere which begin on the 20th of March at midnight until the 24th, inclusively, corresponding to the first decade of the sacred calendar, and to the first genius, named Chontaré, under the influence of Mars: this genius, and those that follow, up to the 8th, belong to the first order of angels which the orthodox call the choir of the Seraphim. He dwells in the region of fire; his sign is the Ram, and he presides over the following five days: the 20th of March, the 31st of April, the 11th of August, the 22nd of October and the 2nd of January; the invocation is made facing the Orient, from midnight precisely until twenty minutes past midnight, to obtain enlightenment. It is by the virtue of these divine names that one becomes illuminated by the spirit of God; they must be pronounced at midnight precisely until twenty minutes past midnight, reciting the third verse of the 3rd psalm (Et tu Domine susceptor meus et gloria mea et exaltans caput meum). One must have one's talisman prepared according to the principles of the cabalistic art. (See on this subject chapter 8.) The person who is born under the influence of this genius has a subtle mind; they are endowed with great sagacity, passionate for the sciences and the arts, capable of undertaking and carrying out the most difficult things; they will love the military profession, because of the influence of Mars; they will have much energy, being dominated by fire.\n\nThe evil genius influences turbulent men; he governs impulsiveness and anger.",
  "2nd Jeliel יליאל. His attribute (God who is helpful). He governs over Turkey (these peoples give to God the name Aydy). His ray begins from the 6th degree up to the 10th, inclusively, corresponding to the influence of the genius named Asican (see the sacred calendar), and to the first decade. He presides over the following days: 21 March, 1 June, 12 August, 23 October, 3 January.\n\nOne invokes this genius to calm popular uprisings, and to obtain victory over those who attack you unjustly. The request must be spoken with the name of the genius, and the 20th verse of Psalm 21 recited. (Tu autem Domine ne elongaveris auxilium tuum a me'ad defensionem meam conspice). The favourable hour begins from twenty minutes past midnight until forty minutes past midnight.\n\nThis genius governs kings and princes; he keeps their subjects in obedience; he has influence over the generation of all beings that exist within the animal kingdom; he restores peace between spouses and conjugal fidelity. Those who are born under this influence have a cheerful mind, agreeable and gallant manners; they will be passionate for women.\n\nThe contrary genius governs all that is harmful to animate beings; he delights in dividing spouses by drawing them away from their duties; he inspires a taste for celibacy and bad morals.",
  "3rd. Sitaël .סיטאל His attribute (God, the hope of all creatures.) His ray begins from the 11th degree of the sphere up to the 15th, inclusively, corresponding to the second decade and to the genius named Chontacré, under the influence of the sun; he presides over the following days: the 22nd of March, the 2nd of June, the 13th of August, the 24th of October, the 4th of January. This genius is invoked against adversities; the request is pronounced with the divine names and the 2nd verse of psalm 90. (Dicet Domino : susceptor meus es tu et refugium meum : Deus meus, sperabo in eum.) The favourable hour begins from forty minutes past midnight until one o'clock. He rules over nobility, magnanimity and high offices; he protects against weapons and fierce beasts. The person who is born under this influence loves the truth; they will keep to their word, and they will take pleasure in obliging those who shall need their services.\n\nThe contrary genius rules hypocrisy, ingratitude and perjury.",
  "4th. Elemiah .עלמיה His attribute is interpreted (Hidden God). He corresponds to the holy name of God Allah, according to the language of the Arabs. His ray begins from the 16th degree of the sphere up to the 20th., inclusively, corresponding to the second decade and to the genius named Sénacher. He presides over the days following: the 23rd of March, the 3rd of June, the 14th of August, the 25th of October, the 5th of January. This genius is invoked against torments of the mind and to know traitors. The request must be pronounced with the 4th verse of the 6th psalm. (Convertere Domine, et eripe animam meam : salvum me fac propter misericordiam tuam.) The favourable hour begins from one o'clock until one hour 20 minutes.\n\nThis genius governs voyages, maritime expeditions, and he influences useful discoveries. The person who is born under this influence will be industrious, fortunate in their undertakings, and will be passionately fond of travel.\n\nThe contrary genius governs bad upbringing, discoveries dangerous to society; he brings hindrance into every undertaking.",
  '5th. Mahasiah .מהשיה His attribute (God the savior). He corresponds to the holy name Teut or Theuth (1), according to the language of the Egyptians. His ray begins from the 21st degree up to the 25th, inclusively, corresponding to the third decade and to the genius named Seket, under the influence of Venus; he presides over the following five days: 24 March, 4 June, 14 August, 26 October, 6 January. The invocation is made from one hour 20 minutes until one hour 40.\n\nThis genius is invoked to live in peace with everyone; one must pronounce the divine names and the 4th verse of psalm 33. (Exquisivi Dominum, et exaudivit me : et ex omnibus tribulationibus meis eripuit me). He governs the high sciences, occult philosophy, theology and the liberal arts. The person who is born under this influence will learn all that they desire with ease; they will have an agreeable countenance and character, and they will be passionate for honest pleasures.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, libertinism, and all the bad qualities of body and mind.\n\n(1) This name is written with four letters in Egyptian characters. The h is not at all a letter, and marks only an aspiration; and the Greek theta forms but one letter.',
  "6th. Lelahel .לׄלּׄהאׄלּׄ Its attribute (God praiseworthy). He corresponds to the name Abgd, according to the language of the Ethiopians. His ray begins from the 26th degree unto the 30th, inclusively, corresponding to the third decade and to the genius named Asentacer; he presides over the following days: 25 March, 5 June, 15 August, 27 October, 7 January. One invokes this genius to acquire knowledge and to cure illnesses; one must recite the 11th verse of psalm 9. (Psallite Domino, qui habitat in Sion : annuntiate inter gentes studia ejus.) The favourable hour begins from 1 hour 40 minutes until 2 o'clock. This genius governs love, renown, the sciences, the arts and fortune. The person who is born under this influence will love to be talked about, and they will acquire celebrity through their talents and actions.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ambition; it drives men to wish to rise above others; it influences all those who seek to acquire fortune by illicit means.",
  "7th. Achaiah .אכאיה Its attribute (Good and patient God). Its ray begins from the 31st degree of the sphere up to the 35th, inclusively, corresponding to the fourth decade and to the genius named Chous, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 26 March, 6 June, 16 August, 28 October, 8 January. The invocation is made from 2 o'clock in the morning until 2 o'clock 20 minutes. One must recite the 8th verse of psalm 102. (Miserator et misericors Dominus : longanimis, et multum misericors.) This genius governs patience; he uncovers the secrets of nature; he has influence over the spread of learning and over industry. The person who is born under this influence will love to instruct themselves in useful things; they will take pride in carrying out the most difficult labours, and they will discover several processes useful to the arts.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of learning; he governs negligence, laziness, and carelessness toward study.",
  '8th. Cahethel .כהתאל His attribute (God adorable). He corresponds to the holy name Moti, according to the language of the Georgians. His ray begins from the 36th degree of the sphere up to the 40th, inclusively, corresponding to the fourth decade and to the genius named Asicat; he presides over the following days: the 27th of March, 7th of June, 17th of August, 29th of October, 9th of January. One invokes the help of this genius by pronouncing the 6th verse of psalm 94. (Venite adoremus, et procidamus: et ploremus ante Dominum, qui fecit nos.) He serves to obtain the blessing of God and to drive away evil spirits. This genius governs all agricultural produce, and principally those which are necessary to the existence of men and animals. He inspires man to raise himself toward God, to thank him for all the goods he sends upon the earth. The person who is born under this influence will love work, agriculture, the countryside and hunting, and they will have much activity in business.\n\nThe evil genius provokes all that is harmful to the produce of the earth; he leads man to blaspheme against God.',
  "9th. Haziel. הזיאל Its attribute (God of mercy). It corresponds to the holy name Agzi, according to the language of the Abyssinians. Its ray begins from the 41st degree up to the 45th, inclusively, corresponding to the fifth decade and to the genius named Erò; under the influence of the moon. This genius and those that follow, up to the 16th, belong to the 2nd order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of the Cherubim. He presides over the following days: 28 March, 8 June, 18 August, 30 October, 10 January. The invocation is made from 2 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 3 o'clock, reciting the 6th verse of psalm 24. (Reminiscere miserationum tuarum, Domine, et misericordiarum tuarum quæ à sæculo sunt.) It serves to obtain the mercy of God, the friendship and favours of the great, and the fulfilment of a promise made by a person. He governs good faith and reconciliation. Those who are born under this influence will be sincere in their promises, and will readily forgive those who have offended them.\n\nThe contrary genius governs hatred and hypocrisy; it influences all those who seek to deceive by every possible means; it makes enemies irreconcilable.",
  "10°. Aladiah .אלדיה His attribute (God propitious). He corresponds to the divine names Siré and Eipi, according to the language of the Persians. His ray begins from the 41st degree up to the 50th, inclusively, corresponding to the fifth decade and to the genius named Viroaso. He presides over the following days: 29 March, 9 June, 19 August, 31 October, 11 January. The invocation is made from 3 o'clock in the morning until three hours 20 minutes, reciting the 22nd verse of psalm 32. (Fiat misericordia tua Domine super nos : quemadmodum speravimus in te.) He is good for those who have hidden crimes and who fear being discovered. This genius rules against rabies and plague, and influences the curing of diseases. The person who is born under this influence will enjoy good health, and they will be fortunate in their undertakings, esteemed by those who know them; they will keep the best company.\n\nThe contrary genius influences those who neglect their health and their affairs.",
  '11°. Lauviah .לאויה Its attribute (God praised and exalted). It corresponds to the holy name Deus, according to the language of the Latins. Its ray begins from the 51st degree of the sphere up to the 55th, inclusively, corresponding to the 6th decade and to the genius named Rombomaré, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 30 March, 10 June, 20 August, 1 November, 12 January. The favourable hour begins from 3 hours 20 minutes until 4 hours. One recites the 50th verse of psalm 17. (Vivit Dominus et benedictus Deus meus, et exultatur Deus salutis meæ.)\n\nIt serves against lightning, and to obtain victory. This genius rules renown; he influences great personages, scholars, and all those who become famous through their talents.\n\nThe contrary genius rules pride, ambition, jealousy and slander.',
  '12°. Hahaiah .הַהַעיה His attribute is interpreted (God refuge.) He corresponds to the holy name Théos, according to the language of the Greeks. His ray begins from the 56th degree of the sphere up to the 60th, inclusively, corresponding to the 6th decade and to the genius named Atarph; he presides over the following days: the 31st of March, the 11th of June, the 22nd of August, the 2nd of November, the 13th of January. The help of this genius is invoked against adversities; you shall pronounce the 22nd verse of psalm 9. (Ut quid Domine recessisti longè, despicis in opportunitatibus, in tribulatione.) The favourable hour begins from 3 hours 40 minutes until 4 hours. He governs dreams, and reveals mysteries hidden from mortals. He influences persons who are wise, spiritual and discreet. The person who is born under this influence has gentle manners, an amiable countenance, and pleasing ways.\n\nThe contrary genius governs indiscretion and lying; he influences all those who abuse the trust of others.',
  "13°. Iezalel .יזּלּׄאׄלּ His attribute (God glorified above all things). He corresponds to the holy name of God Boog, according to the language of the Illyrians. His ray begins from the 61st degree of the sphere up to the 65th, inclusively, corresponding to the 7th decade and to the genius named Théosolk, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the days hereafter: the 1st of April, the 12th of June, the 23rd of August, the 3rd of September, the 14th of January. The favourable hour begins from 4 o'clock until 4 o'clock 20 minutes. One must recite the 6th verse of psalm 97. (Jubilate Deo omnis terra: cantate, et exultate, et psallite) He governs friendship, reconciliation, and conjugal fidelity. The person who is born under this influence will learn all they wish with ease; they will have a retentive memory, and will distinguish themselves by their skill.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, error and lying, and influences narrow minds who wish to learn nothing nor do anything.",
  '14th. Mebahel מבהאל. His attribute (God the preserver). He corresponds to the holy name Dios, according to the Spanish language. His ray begins from the 66th degree up to the 10th, inclusively, corresponding to the 7th decade, and to the genius named Thésogar. He presides over the following days: 2 April, 13 June, 24 August, 4 November, 15 January. This genius is invoked against those who seek to usurp the fortune of others; one must recite the 9th verse of psalm 9. (Et factus est Dominus refugium pauperis : adjutor in opportunitatibus, in tribulatione.) The favourable hour begins from 4 hours 20 minutes up to 4 hours 40. He governs justice, truth and liberty; he delivers the oppressed and prisoners; he protects innocence and makes truth known. The person who is born under this influence will love jurisprudence, and they will distinguish themselves at the bar.\n\nThe contrary genius governs slander, false testimony and legal proceedings.',
  '15th. Hariel הריאל. His attribute (God creator). He corresponds to the divine names Idio or Iddio, according to the Italian language. His ray begins from the 71st degree up to the 75th, inclusively, corresponding to the 8th decade and to the genius named Ouêrê, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 3 April, 14 June, 25 August, 5 November, 16 January. This genius is invoked against the impious of religion; their names are pronounced with the divine names and the 22nd verse of psalm 93. (Et factus est mihi Dominus in refugium: et Deus meus in adjutorium spei meæ.) The favourable hour begins from 4 hours 40 minutes until 5 hours. This genius governs over the sciences and the arts; he influences useful discoveries and new methods. The person who is born under this influence will love the company of good people; they will have religious feelings, and they will distinguish themselves by the purity of their morals.\n\nThe contrary genius governs schisms, wars of religion; it influences the impious and all those who propagate dangerous sects, and who seek the means of establishing new ones.',
  "16th. Hakamiah הקמיה. His attribute (God who erects the universe.) He governs France, and corresponds to the name God, according to the language of that nation. His ray begins from the 76th degree of the sphere up to the 80th, inclusively, corresponding to the 8th decade and to the genius named Vérasua, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 4 April, 15 June, 26 August, 6 November, 17 January. This genius is invoked against traitors, to obtain victory over the enemy, and to be delivered from those who wish to oppress us; one must pronounce their names with what follows: O God almighty of hosts, thou who erects the universe, and who protects the French nation, I invoke thee, I so-and-so, by the name of Hakamiah, that thou mayest deliver France from her enemies. You shall then pronounce the first mysterious verse of psalm 87. (Domine Deus salutis meæ, in die clamavi, et nocte coram te.) This prayer must be recited every day, the face turned toward the east, from 5 o'clock in the morning until 5 o'clock 20 minutes. This genius governs crowned heads and great captains; he gives victory, and forestalls seditions; he has influence over iron, arsenals, and all that pertains to military engineering. The man who is born under this influence is of a frank, loyal and brave character, sensitive on the point of honor, faithful to his oath, and passionate for Venus.\n\nThe contrary genius governs traitors; he provokes betrayals, sedition and revolt.",
  "17th. Lauviah. לאויה His attribute (God admirable). He corresponds to the name Goth, according to the language of the Germans. His ray begins from the 81st degree of the sphere up to the 85th, inclusively, corresponding to the ninth decade and to the genius named Phuor, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 5 April, 16 June, 27 August, 7 November, 18 January. This genius and those that follow up to the 24th belong to the 3rd order of angels named the choir of thrones. The invocation is made, every day while fasting, from 5 o'clock in the morning until 5 hours 20 minutes: one must pronounce the 1st verse of psalm 8. (Domine Deus noster, quam admirabile est nomen tuum in universâ terrâ!) It serves against torments of the spirit, sadness, and for resting well at night. He governs the high sciences, marvelous discoveries, and gives revelations in dreams. The person who is born under this influence will love music, poetry, literature and philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs atheism, impious philosophers, and all those who attack the dogmas of religion.",
  "18th. Caliel. כליאל His attribute is interpreted (God prompt to hear). He corresponds to the name Boog, according to the language of the Poles. His ray begins from the 86th degree of the sphere up to the 90th, corresponding to the ninth decade and to the genius named Tepisatosoa; he presides over the following days, namely: the 6th of April, 17th of June, 28th of August, 8th of November, 18th of January. This genius is invoked to obtain prompt help when some adversity occurs; one must recite the 9th verse of psalm 7. (Judica me Domine secundum justitiam meam, et secundum innocentiam meam super me.) The favourable hour begins from five hours 40 minutes in the morning until 6 o'clock. This genius makes the truth known in legal proceedings, he causes innocence to triumph, he confounds the guilty and false witnesses. The person who is born under this influence will be just and upright, will love truth, and they will distinguish themselves in the magistracy.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over scandalous lawsuits, he influences vile, base, and grovelling men, and those who seek to tangle up affairs and enrich themselves at the expense of their clients.",
  "19th Leuviah. לּׄוויׄה. His attribute (God who hears sinners). He corresponds to the name Bogy, according to the language of the Hungarians. He governs the first ray of the south, which begins from the 91st degree of the sphere up to the 95th, inclusively, corresponding to the tenth decade and to the genius named Sotis, under the influence of Venus; he presides over the following days: the 7th of April, the 18th of June, the 29th of August, the 9th of November, the 20th of January. The help of this genius is invoked facing south, from 6 o'clock in the morning until 6 hours 20 minutes, reciting the 1st verse of psalm 39. (Expectans expectavi Dominum, et intendit mihi.) It serves to obtain the grace of God. This genius governs the memory and the intelligence of man. The person who is born under this influence will be amiable and cheerful, modest in their words, and simple in their manner of being; they will bear adversities with resignation and much patience.\n\nThe contrary genius influences griefs, losses, and mortifications; it provokes debauchery and despair.",
  '20th. Pahaliah. פהליה. His attribute (God the redeemer). He corresponds to the holy name Tios, according to the language of the Muscovites. His ray begins from the 95th degree of the sphere up to the 100th, inclusively, corresponding to the tenth decade and to the genius named Sothis; he presides over the 8th of April, the 19th of June, the 30th of August, the 10th of November, the 21st of January, which correspond to the influence of Venus. (See the sacred calendar, page 41.) The invocation is made from 6 hours 20 minutes until 6 hours 40 minutes; the 2nd verse of psalm 119 must be recited. (Domine libera animam meam à labiis iniquis, et à linguâ dolosâ.) He serves against the enemies of religion, and to convert peoples to Christianity. This genius governs religion, theology and morals; it influences chastity and piety, and those whose calling is to the ecclesiastical state.\n\nThe contrary genius governs irreligion, apostates, libertines and renegades.',
  "21st Nelchael .נלכאל His attribute (God alone and unique). He corresponds to the name Bueg, according to the language of the Bohemians. His ray begins from the 101st degree of the sphere up to the 105th, inclusively, corresponding to the 11th decade and to the genius named Sith, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 9 April, 20 June, 31 August, 11 November, 22 January. The invocation is made from 6 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 7 o'clock. One must pronounce the 18th verse of psalm 30. (Ego autem in te speravi Domine : dixi Deus meus es tu : in manibus tuis sortes meæ.) It serves against slanderers, charms, and to destroy the power of evil spirits. This genius governs astronomy, mathematics, geography, and all the abstract sciences; he influences the learned and philosophers. The person who is born under this influence will love poetry, literature, and will be passionate about study; they will distinguish themselves in mathematics and geometry.\n\nThe evil genius governs ignorance, error, and prejudices.",
  "22nd. Ieiaiel .יׄיׄיׄאׄלּׄ Its attribute (the right hand of God). It corresponds to the holy name Good, according to the English language. Its ray begins from the 106th degree of the sphere up to the 110th, inclusively, corresponding to the 11th decade and to the genius named Syth, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 10 April, 21 June, 1 September, 12 November, 22 January. The invocation is made from seven o'clock until 7 hours 20 minutes; one recites the 3rd verse of psalm 120. (Dominus custodit te; Dominus protectio tua, super manum dexteram tuam.) This genius governs fortune, renown, diplomacy and commerce; he has influence over travels, discoveries, and maritime expeditions; he protects against storms and shipwrecks. The person who is born under this influence will love commerce, will be industrious, and they will distinguish themself by their liberal and philanthropic ideas.\n\nThe contrary genius governs pirates, corsairs and slaves; he has influence over maritime expeditions.",
  "23rd. Melahel .מלּׄהאׄלּׄ His attribute (God who delivers from evils). He corresponds to the name Dieh, according to the language of the Hibernians. His ray begins from the 111th degree of the sphere up to the 115th inclusively, corresponding to the 12th decade and to the genius named Chumis, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 11 April, 22 June, 2 September, 13 November, 24 January. The invocation is made from 7 o'clock 20 minutes in the morning until 7 o'clock 40, reciting the 8th verse of psalm 120. (Dominus custodiat introïtum tuum, et exitum tuum : et ex hoc nunc, et in sæculum.) He serves against weapons, and for traveling in safety. This genius governs water, all the productions of the earth, and principally the plants that are necessary for the healing of illnesses. The person who is born under this influence is of a bold nature, and capable of undertaking the most perilous expeditions; they will distinguish themself through honorable actions.\n\nThe contrary genius influences everything that is harmful to vegetation; he causes illnesses and plague.",
  '24°. Hahiuiah .ההויה His attribute (God good by Himself). He corresponds to the holy name Esar, according to the language of the Etruscans. His ray begins from the 116th degree of the sphere up to the 120th, inclusively, corresponding to the 12th decade and to the genius named Thuimis. He presides over the following days: 12 April, 23 June, 3 September, 14 November, 25 January. The invocation is made from 7 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 8 hours: one pronounces the divine names with the 18th verse of psalm 32. (Ecce oculi Domini super metuentes eum : et in eis, qui sperant in misericordia ejus.). It serves to obtain the grace and mercy of God. This genius rules over exiles, fugitive prisoners, those condemned in absentia; he prevents the discovery of secret crimes, and those who have committed them will escape the justice of men, provided they do not fall again into the same fault; he protects against harmful animals, and he preserves from thieves and murderers. Those who are born under this influence love truth, the exact sciences; they are sincere in their words and their actions.\n\nThe contrary genius rules all harmful beings; it drives men to commit crimes, and influences all those who seek to live by unlawful means.',
  "25th. Nith-Haiah נתהיה. His attribute (God who gives wisdom.) He corresponds to the holy name of God Orsy, according to the language of the Magi. His ray begins from the 121st degree of the sphere up to the 125th, inclusively, corresponding to the 13th decade and to the genius named Charcumis, under the influence of Saturn. This genius and those that follow, up to the 32nd, belong to the 4th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of dominations. He presides over the following days: 13 April, 24 June, 4 September, 15 November, 26 January. The invocation is made from 8 o'clock until 8 hours 20 minutes; you shall pronounce the divine names with the 1st verse of psalm 9. (Confitebor tibi Domine in toto corde meo : narrabo omnia mirabilia tua.) He serves to have wisdom, and to discover the truth of hidden mysteries. This genius rules all the occult sciences; he gives revelations in dreams, and particularly to those who are born on the day he presides; he has influence over wise men who love peace and solitude, and over those who seek truth and practise the magic of the wise, which is that of God (1).\n\nThe contrary genius rules black magic, that of the evil principle, the demon; it consists in making a pact with him, by which one engages to renounce God, to do harm to men, to animals, and to the produce of the earth.\n\n(1) Modern philosophers call it the Science of Christ and of man.",
  "26th. Haaiah. האאיה. Its attribute (Hidden God). He corresponds to the sacred divine names, Agdy and Abdi, according to the language of the Saracens. His ray begins from the 126th degree up to the 130th, inclusively, corresponding to the 13th decade and to the genius named Aphruimis. He presides over the following days: 14 April, 25 June, 5 September, 16 November, 27 January. The invocation is made from 20 minutes past 8 in the morning until 8:40. One must pronounce the divine names and the 145th verse of psalm 118. (Clamavi in toto corde meo, exaudi me Domine; justificationes tuas requiram.) He serves for winning one's lawsuit and for making the judges favorable to oneself. This genius protects all who seek the truth; he leads men to the contemplation of divine things; he governs politics, diplomats, plenipotentiaries, ambassadors, treaties of peace and commerce, and all conventions in general: he has influence over couriers, dispatches, agents, and secret expeditions.\n\nThe contrary genius governs traitors, the ambitious, and conspiracies.",
  "27th. Ierathel .ירתאל His attribute (God who punishes the wicked). He corresponds to the holy name Téos, according to the language of the Copts. His ray begins from the 131st degree of the sphere up to the 135th, inclusively, corresponding to the 14th decade, and to the genius named Hépê, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the following days: 15 April, 26 June, 6 September, 17 November, 28 January. The invocation is made from 8 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 9 o'clock. One pronounces the divine names and the 1st verse of psalm 139. (Eripe me Domine ab homine malo, à viro iniquo eripe me.) He serves to confound the wicked and slanderers, and to be delivered from our enemies. This genius protects against those who provoke us and attack us unjustly. He governs the spread of learning, civilization and liberty. The person who is born under this influence will love peace, justice, the sciences and the arts, and they will distinguish themselves in literature.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ignorance, slavery and intolerance.",
  "28th. Séheiah .שאׄהיׄה His attribute (God who heals the sick). He corresponds to the holy name (1) Adad אדאד, according to the language of the Assyrians. His ray begins from the 136th degree up to the 140th, exclusively, corresponding to the 14th decade and to the genius named Sithacer. He presides over the following days: 16 April, 27 June, 7 September, 18 November, 29 January. The invocation is made from 9 o'clock in the morning until 9 hours 20 minutes. One must pronounce the divine names with the 13th verse of psalm 70. (Deus ne elongeris à me : Deus meus in auxilium meum respice.) He serves against infirmities and thunder. This genius protects against fires, ruin of buildings, falls, illnesses, etc. He governs health and length of life. The person who is born under this influence will have much judgment; they will act only with prudence and circumspection.\n\nThe contrary genius governs catastrophes, accidents, and causes apoplexies; he influences persons who never reflect before acting.\n\n(1) The name Adad signifies alone; it comes from the word sol, which designates the sun, to which he corresponds.",
  '29th. Reiiel .ריׄיׄאׄלּׄ Its attribute (God prompt to help) and corresponds to the holy name Zimi, according to the language of the Peruvians. Its ray begins from the 141st degree of the sphere up to the 145th, inclusively, corresponding to the 15th decade and to the genius named Phupé, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 17 April, 28 June, 8 September, 19 November, 30 January. The invocation is made from 9 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 9 hours 40. One must pronounce the divine names with the request and the 4th verse of psalm 53. (Ecce enim Deus adjuvat me : et Dominus susceptor est animæ meæ.) It serves against the impious and the enemies of religion, and to be delivered from all their enemies both visible and invisible. This genius governs all religious sentiments, divine philosophy, and meditation. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves by their virtues and their zeal to propagate the truth; they will make every effort to destroy impiety by their writings and by their example.\n\nThe contrary genius governs fanaticism and hypocrisy; it influences all those who spread irreligion through writings and dangerous maxims.',
  '30°. Omael. ומאאל His attribute (God who is patient.) He corresponds to the name Tura, according to the language of the Indians. His ray begins from the 146th degree of the sphere up to the 150th, inclusively, corresponding to the 9th decade and to the genius named Phuonisié. He presides over the following days: 28 April, 29 June, 9 September, 20 November, 3ł January. The invocation is made from 9 hours 40 minutes in the morning until 10 hours: one pronounces the divine names and the 6th verse of psalm 70. (Quoniam tu es patientia mea Domine: Domine spes mea à juventute mea.) He serves against sorrows, despair, and to have patience. This genius rules over the animal kingdom; he watches over the generation of beings, so as to multiply their species and perpetuate their races; he has influence over chemists, physicians, and surgeons. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself in anatomy and medicine.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of the propagation of beings; he has influence over monstrous phenomena.',
  "31st. Lecabel .לכבאל His attribute (God who inspires.) He corresponds to the holy name Teli, according to the language of the Chinese. His ray begins from the 151st degree up to the 155th, corresponding to the 16th decade and to the genius named Tomi, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 19 April, 30 June, 10 September, 21 November, 1 February. The help of Lecabel is invoked to have knowledge, and for methods useful to the profession one practises. The invocation is made from 10 o'clock in the morning until 10 o'clock 20 minutes. The request must be pronounced with the divine names and the 16th mysterious verse of psalm 70. (Quoniam non cognovi litteraturam, introïbo in potentias Domini : Domine memorabor justitiæ tuæ solius). He governs vegetation and agriculture. The person who is born under this influence will love astronomy, mathematics and geometry; they will be distinguished by their luminous ideas, and will solve the most difficult problems, and will owe their fortune only to their talents.\n\nThe contrary genius governs avarice and usury; he influences all those who enrich themselves by unlawful means.",
  '32nd. Vasariah .ושריה His attribute (God just.) He corresponds to the name Anot, according to the language of the Tartars. His ray begins from the 156th degree of the sphere up to the 160th, inclusively, corresponding to the 16th decade and to the genius named Thumis. He presides over the following days: 20 April, 1 July, 11 September, 22 November, 2 February: One invokes the aid of this genius against those who attack us in a court of justice (1), and to obtain pardon for those who have recourse to the clemency of kings; for this purpose one must name the name of the person who attacks you, and cite the motive; then pronounce the divine names with the 4th verse of psalm 32. (Quia rectum est verbum Domini, et omnia opera ejus in fide.) The favourable hour begins from 10 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 10 hours 40. This genius rules justice; he has influence over nobility, jurisconsults, magistrates and lawyers. The person who is born under this influence will have a retentive memory and will speak with ease, they will be amiable, witty and modest.\n\nThe contrary genius rules all the bad qualities of the body and of the soul.\n\n(1) If the person attacked recognizes in their soul and conscience that they are in the wrong, they must accordingly invoke this genius to come to an amicable arrangement with the adverse party, without which they would not succeed.',
  '33rd. Iehuiah יהויה. His attribute (God who knows all things.) He corresponds to the holy name Agad, according to the language of the Hesperides. His ray begins from the 161st degree of the sphere up to the 165th, inclusively, corresponding to the 17th decade and to the genius named Ouestucati, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 21 April, 2 July, 12 September, 23 November, 3 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 40th, belong to the 5th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of Powers. The invocation is made from 10 hours 40 minutes until 11 hours; one must pronounce the 11th verse of psalm 33. (Dominus scit cogitationes hominum quoniam vanæ sunt.) He serves to know traitors, to destroy their projects and their machinations. This genius protects all Christian princes; he maintains their subjects in obedience. The person who is born under this influence will love to fulfill all the duties of their station.\n\nThe contrary genius dominates all insubordinate beings; he provokes the seditious to revolt.',
  "34th. Lehahiah .לּׄההיׄה His attribute (Merciful God.) He corresponds to the name Aneb, according to the language of the peoples of the Congo. His ray begins from the 166th degree of the sphere up to the 170th, inclusively, corresponding to the 17th decade and to the genius named Thopitus. He presides over the days set out hereafter: 22 April, 3 July, 13 September, 24 November, 4 February. The invocation is made from 11 o'clock in the morning until 11 o'clock 20 minutes, reciting the 5th verse of psalm 130. (Speret Israël in Domino; ex hoc nunc, et usque in sæculum.) He serves against anger. This genius rules over crowned heads, princes and nobles; he maintains harmony, good understanding and peace between them; he influences the obedience of subjects towards their princes. The person who is born under this influence will become renowned for their talents and their actions; they will have the trust and favours of their prince, which they will merit through their devotion, their fidelity, and the great services which they will render to him.\n\nThe contrary genius rules discord; he provokes war, betrayals, and the ruin of nations.",
  '35th. Chavakiah .כוקיה His attribute (God who gives joy.) He corresponds to the name Anup. His ray begins from the 171st degree up to the 175th, inclusively, corresponding to the 18th decade and to the genius named Aphoso, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following days: 23 April, 4 July, 14 September, 25 November, 5 February. One invokes the help of this genius in order to be restored to grace with those one has offended; for this purpose one must pronounce the request, the divine names, and name the person; then you will say the 1st verse of psalm 114. (Dilexi quoniam exaudiet Dominus vocem orationis meæ.) It must be recited every day, until you are reconciled with the person. The favourable hour begins from 11 hours 20 minutes in the morning until 11 hours 40. This genius rules over wills, inheritances, and all divisions of property made amicably; he maintains peace and harmony in families. The person who is born under this influence loves to live in peace with everyone, even at the expense of their own interests; they make it a duty to reward the fidelity and good care of those attached to their service.\n\nThe contrary genius causes discord in family arrangements; he provokes unjust and ruinous lawsuits.',
  "36th. Menadel מנדאל. His attribute (God adorable). He corresponds to the holy name Alla, according to the language of the Moors. His ray begins from the 176th degree of the sphere up to the 180th, inclusively, corresponding to the 18th decade and to the genius named Aphut. He presides over the five days following: 24 April, 5 July, 15 September, 26 November, 6 February. This genius is invoked to be maintained in one's employment, and to preserve the means of existence one possesses: the request is uttered with the divine names and the 8th verse of psalm 25. (Domine dilexi decorem domus tuæ : et locum habitationis gloriæ tuæ.) He serves against calumnies and to deliver prisoners. The favourable hour begins from 11 o'clock 40 minutes in the morning until noon precisely. This genius gives knowledge concerning absent persons from whom no news has been received for a long time; he causes exiles to return to their homeland, and discovers goods lost or misappropriated.\n\nThe contrary genius protects all those who seek to flee abroad to escape justice.",
  '37°. Aniel .אׄנואלּ His attribute (God of virtues). He corresponds to the holy name of God Abda, according to the ancient Philosophers. His ray begins from the 181st degree of the sphere up to the 185th, inclusively, corresponding to the 19th decade and to the genius named Souchoë, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 25 April, 6 July, 16 September, 27 November, 7 February. The invocation is made from noon until twenty minutes past noon; one pronounces the divine names and the 8th verse of psalm 79. (Deus ad virtutem converte nos : et ostende faciem tuam et salvi erimus.) He serves to obtain victory and to make an army lift the siege of a town. This genius rules over the sciences and the arts; he reveals the secrets of nature, and inspires wise philosophers in their meditations. The person who is born under this influence will acquire celebrity through their talents and their knowledge, and they will be distinguished among the learned.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over perverse spirits; he has influence over charlatans and over all those who excel in the art of deceiving men.',
  "38°. Haamiah, העמיה. His attribute (God, the hope of all the children of the earth). He corresponds to the great name of God Agla אֶגְלָא (God threefold and one). According to the cabalists, this name is drawn from that mysterious verse of Scripture אתה גיבר לעולם אדני, which signifies in French: Thou art the strong God through eternity (1). It is composed of the first letters of these four words, beginning from right to left (2). The ray of this genius begins from the 186th degree of the sphere up to the 190th, inclusively, corresponding to the 19th decade and to the genius named Serucuth. He presides over the following days: 26 April, 7 July, 17 September, 28 November, 8 February. These divine names are invoked to acquire all the treasures of heaven and earth; one must recite the 9th verse of psalm 90. (Quoniam tu es Domine spes mea : altissimum posuisti refugium tuum.) The cabalists say that this psalm serves against lightning, weapons, ferocious animals, and internal spirits. (See the cabala of the psalms.) This genius governs all religious worship, and all that relates to God; he protects all those who seek the truth.\n\nThe contrary genius governs error and lying, and influences all those who hold no principle of religion.\n\n(1) See Agrippa, in the 3rd book of his Occult Philosophy, p. 41. At The Hague, 1727. It is also found in Kircher. Œdipus Ægyptiacus, volume 2, p. 115.\n\n(2) By this means you have the key to the 72 Hebrew verses which are written around the talismans of the 72 genii, which are found in the cabalistic sphere. Each of these verses contains the name of God and the attribute of the genius to which it corresponds.\n\nThe Abbé de Villars recounts marvellous things, speaking of the great name AGLA, in his work entitled the Comte de Gabalis (see the third conversation). The best edition is that of Amsterdam, at Jacques Lejeune's, in 1700. He asserts that with this name one works an infinity of marvels, even when pronounced by a profane mouth; he claims that those who wish to convince themselves of the truth must exalt their imagination and their faith, then turn toward the east, observing on this subject all that is indicated in the cabalistic rite...\n\nThe wise philosophers say that this name was revealed to Jacob, when he saw in a dream the ladder of 72 rungs, with the 72 angels who went up and down toward the place called the gate of heaven, and they claim that it was by it that Joseph was delivered from his brothers, and that he interpreted dreams, notably that of Pharaoh.\n\nThe cabalists write this name upon the mysterious wand which is used in cabalistic experiments, and here is how it is made: one must cut a branch grown that same year, of virgin hazel or filbert, that is to say the tree must never have borne fruit, and no branch must ever have been cut or broken, which is easily found in a shrub of new growth; it is cut between eleven and twelve o'clock at night, under influences favourable to the experiment one wishes to make; one must have a new knife, which has never been used, and draw it upward while cutting the wand, and pronounce certain words, the face turned toward the east; then it must be blessed, and one writes on the thicker end the name AGLA, in the middle the word ON, and on the thinner end the name TETRAGRAMMATON; these three names must each be accompanied by a cross and their mysterious character; and when they are about to proceed to the evocations, they strike the air in a cross with this wand, toward the four parts of the world beginning with the east, then toward the south, afterward toward the west, and toward the north, pronouncing each time what follows: I......, I conjure thee, Genius......, to obey me at once; by the living God, by the true God, by the holy God, and they strike the air each time, forming the cross.\n\nAs everyone knows the analogy of the circular figure with unity, which is the perfect symbol of God, it is for this reason that one must enclose oneself within this mysterious character and in the midst of a triangle, each time one proceeds to the evocations. (See the Frontispiece.)",
  "39th. Rehael רהעאׄלּׄ. His attribute (God who receives sinners). He corresponds to the holy name Goot, according to the language of the Scots. His ray begins from the 191st degree of the sphere up to the 195th, inclusively, corresponding to the 20th decade and to the genius named Ptéchout, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 27 April, 8 July, 18 September, 29 November, 9 February. The invocation is made from forty minutes past noon until one o'clock. One must recite the 13th verse of psalm 29. (Audivit Dominus, et misertus est mei : Dominus factus est meus adjutor.) It serves for the healing of sicknesses and to obtain the mercy of God. This genius governs health and length of life; he influences paternal and filial love, and the obedience and respect of children toward their parents.\n\nThe contrary genius is named Terre-Morte or Terre-Damnée, according to the expression of Etteilla, in his Philosophie des Hautes-Sciences, page 83. He is the most cruel and most treacherous that is known; he influences infanticides and parricides.",
  "40th. Ieiazel. יׄיׄזּאׄלּׄ His attribute (God who gives joy). He corresponds to the holy name Goed, according to the language of the Belgians. His ray begins from the 196th degree of the sphere up to the 200th, inclusively, corresponding to the 20th decade and to the genius named Aterchinis. He presides over the following five days: the 28th of April, the 9th of July, the 19th of September, the 30th of November, the 10th of February. The invocation is made from one o'clock in the afternoon until twenty minutes past one. The request is pronounced with the divine names and the 15th verse of psalm 87. (Ut quid Domine repellis orationem meam : avertis faciem tuam à me.) This psalm has marvellous properties; it serves to deliver prisoners, to obtain consolations, and to be delivered from one's enemies. This genius governs printing and bookselling; he influences men of letters and artists. The person who is born under this influence will love reading, drawing, and all the sciences in general.\n\nThe evil genius governs all the bad qualities of the body and soul; he influences gloomy minds and those who flee society.",
  '41st. Hahahel .הההאׄלּׄ. Its attribute (God in three persons). It corresponds to the holy name Gudi, according to the Irish language. Its ray begins from the 201st degree of the sphere up to the 205th, inclusively, corresponding to the 21st decade and to the genius named Chontaré, under the influence of Jupiter. It presides over the following days: 29 April, 10 July, 20 September, 1 December, 11 February. This genius, and those that follow, up to the 48th, belong to the 5th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of virtues. This genius is invoked (1) from twenty past one in the afternoon until twenty to two, pronouncing the 2nd verse of psalm 119. (Domine libera animam meam à labiis iniquis, et à linguâ dolosâ.) It serves against the enemies of religion, the impious, and slanderers. This genius governs Christianity; it protects missionaries and all the disciples of Christ, who announce the words of the Gospel to the nations; it influences pious souls, prelates, ecclesiastics, and all that relates to the priesthood. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their greatness of soul and their energy; they will consecrate themselves entirely to the service of God, and they will not fear to suffer martyrdom for Christ.\n\nThe contrary genius influences apostates, renegades, and all those who dishonor the priesthood by their scandalous conduct.\n\n(1) Note that those who resort to this genius in their prayers must pay close attention to its attribute and its influence; for if you make to it a request contrary to its attributes, it will not succeed.',
  "42nd. Mikael מיכאל. The cabalists give him the following attributes: virtue of God, house of God, similar to God. He corresponds to the name Biub or Biud, according to the language of the Canadians. His ray begins from the 216th degree of the sphere up to the 210th inclusively, corresponding to the 21st decade and to the genius named Arpien. He presides over the following days: 30 April, 11 July, 21 September, 2 December, 12 February. The invocation is made from 1 hour 40 minutes until 2 o'clock exactly; one pronounces the request with the divine names and the 7th verse of psalm 120 (Dominus custodit te ab omni malo; custodiat animam tuam Dominus.) He serves for travelling in safety. This genius influences monarchs, princes, and nobles; he keeps their subjects in obedience, uncovers conspiracies, and all those who seek to destroy their persons and their governments. The person who is born under this influence will occupy themselves with political affairs; they will be curious, will want to know the secrets of the cabinets and foreign news, and they will distinguish themselves in affairs of state through their knowledge of diplomacy.\n\nThe contrary genius dominates traitors; he influences malevolence, and all those who spread false news.",
  "43rd. Veualiah וולּּׄיׄה. Its attribute (Ruling King). It corresponds to the holy name Solu, according to the language of the Californians. Its ray begins from the 211th degree of the sphere up to the 215th, inclusively, corresponding to the 22nd decade and to the genius named Stochêné, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the following days: 1 May, 12 July, 22 September, 3 December, 13 February. The invocation is made from 2 o'clock in the afternoon until 2 hours 20 minutes, pronouncing the 14th verse of psalm 87. (Et ego ad te Domine clamavi : et manè oratio mea prœveniet te.) It serves to destroy the enemy and to be delivered from slavery. This genius presides over peace, and influences the prosperity of empires; it strengthens tottering thrones and the power of kings. The person who is born under this influence will love the military life and glory; they will occupy themselves constantly with the sciences that are related to the genius of war; they will become famous by their feats of arms, and will acquire the trust of their prince by the services which they will render him.\n\nThe evil genius sows discord between princes; it influences the destruction of empires; it maintains revolutions and party spirits.",
  '44th. Ielahiah יְלָהִיָה. His attribute (Eternal God). He corresponds to the holy name Bosa, according to the language of the Mexicans. His ray begins from the 216th degree of the sphere up to the 220th, inclusively, corresponding to the 22nd decade and to the genius named Sentacer. He presides over the following days: 2 May, 13 July, 23 September, 4 December, 14 February. This genius is invoked to obtain the success of a useful undertaking; the request must be spoken with the divine names and the 108th verse of Psalm 118. (Voluntaria oris mei bene placita fac Domine: et judicia tua doce me.) It is good for having the protection of magistrates and for winning a lawsuit. This genius protects against weapons; he gives victory. The person who is born under this influence will love to travel in order to learn, and all their undertakings will succeed for them; they will distinguish themselves by their military talents and their bravery, and their name will become famous in the annals of glory.\n\nThe contrary genius presides over war, and causes all the scourges that follow from it; he influences all those who violate terms of surrender and massacre their prisoners without pity.',
  "45th. Sealiah סאׄלּׄיׄה. His attribute (Mover of all things.) He corresponds to the holy name Hobo, according to the language of the peoples of Quito. His ray begins from the 221st degree of the sphere up to the 225th, corresponding to the 23rd decade and to the genius named Sesmê, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 3 May, 14 July, 24 September, 5 December, 15 February. The invocation is made from 2 o'clock 40 minutes in the afternoon until 3 o'clock. One must pronounce the 18th verse of psalm 93. (Si dicebam, motus est pes meus : misericordia tua Domine adjuvabat me.) He serves to confound the wicked and the proud; he raises up those who are humbled and fallen. This genius rules over vegetation; he carries life and health into all that breathes, and influences the chief agents of nature. The person who is born under this influence will love to learn; they will have great abilities and much facility.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over the atmosphere; he provokes great heat or great cold, great droughts or excessive humidity.",
  "36th. Ariel עריׄאׄלּׄ. His attribute (God who reveals). He corresponds to the holy name Pino, according to the language of the peoples of Paraguay. His ray begins from the 226th degree of the sphere up to the 130th, inclusively, corresponding to the 23rd decade and to the genius named Tépiseuth. He presides over the following days: 4 May, 15 July, 25 September, 6 December, 16 February. This genius is invoked in order to have revelations; the request is pronounced with the divine names and the 9th verse of psalm 144. (Suavis Dominus universis: et miserationes ejus super omnia opera ejus.) He serves to thank God for the good things he sends us. The favourable hour begins from 3 o'clock in the afternoon until 3 o'clock 20 minutes. This genius discovers hidden treasures; he reveals the greatest secrets of nature, and he causes to be seen in dream the objects that one desires. The person who is born under this influence is endowed with a strong and subtle mind; they will have new ideas and sublime thoughts; they will succeed in resolving the most difficult problems; they will be discreet and will act with great circumspection.\n\nThe contrary genius causes troubles of the mind; it leads men to commit the greatest inconsistencies, and has influence over weak minds.",
  '47th. Asaliah .עּשלּׄיׄה His attribute (God just, who reveals the truth). He corresponds to the name Hana, according to the language of the peoples of Chile. His ray begins from the 231st degree up to the 235th, inclusively, corresponding to the 24th decade and to the genius named Siêmé, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 5 May, 16 July, 26 September, 7 December, 17 February. The invocation is made from twenty past three in the afternoon until twenty to four, while pronouncing the 25th verse of psalm 104. (Quàm magnificata sunt opera tua Domine! omnia in sapientia fecisti : impleta est terra possessione tua.) He serves to praise God and to raise oneself towards him when he sends us knowledge. This genius governs justice, and makes the truth known in legal proceedings; he has influence over upright men, and over those who raise their mind to the contemplation of divine things. The person who is born under this influence is endowed with an agreeable character; they will be passionate to acquire secret knowledge.\n\nThe contrary genius governs immoral and scandalous actions, and all those who propagate dangerous and chimerical systems.',
  "48th. Mihael מיהאל His attribute (God, helpful father). He corresponds to the holy name Zaca (1), according to the language of the Japanese. His ray begins from the 236th degree of the sphere up to the 240th, inclusively, corresponding to the 24th decade and to the genius named Senciner. He presides over the five days following: 6 May, 17 July, 27 September, 8 December, 18 February. The invocation is made from twenty past three in the afternoon until four o'clock, pronouncing the 3rd verse of psalm 97. (Notum fecit Dominus salutare suum: in conspectu gentium revelavit justitiam suam.) He serves to preserve peace and union between spouses. This genius protects those who have recourse to him; they will have presentiments and secret inspirations concerning all that shall befall them. He rules over the generation of beings, and he influences friendship and conjugal fidelity. The person who is born under this influence will be passionate for love; they will love walking and all pleasures in general.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over luxury, sterility and inconstancy; he sets discord between spouses, and he causes jealousy and unease.\n\n(1) The holy name Zaca corresponds to the name Zacael and to psalm 41, quemadmodum, etc. (See on this subject the cabala of the psalms.) It serves to deliver souls from purgatory, to acquire all spiritual and temporal goods, and to have revelations in dreams. It is necessary that the request be just and that it be pleasing to God.",
  "49th. Vehuel והואל. Its attribute (God great and exalted). It corresponds to the holy name of God Mara, according to the language of the inhabitants of the Philippine Islands. Its ray begins from the 241st degree of the sphere up to the 245th, inclusively, corresponding to the 25th decade and to the genius named Rêuo, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following five days: 7 May, 18 July, 28 September, 9 December, 19 February. This genius and those which follow, up to the 56th, belong to the 7th order of angels, which the orthodox call the choir of principalities. The invocation is made from ♆ o'clock in the afternoon until ♆ o'clock 20 minutes; one pronounces the request with the divine names and the 3rd verse of psalm 144. (Magnus Dominus et laudabilis nimis et magnitudinis ejus non est finis.) One must recite this psalm entirely, when one experiences sorrows and when one's mind is troubled. It serves to raise oneself toward God, to bless and glorify Him, when one is touched by admiration. This genius rules over great personages, and over all those who rise up and distinguish themselves by their talents and their virtues. The person who is born under this influence will have a sensitive and generous soul; they will be esteemed by all good people for their virtues and their good deeds; they will distinguish themselves in literature, jurisprudence, and diplomacy.\n\nThe contrary genius influences selfish men; it rules over hatred and hypocrisy.",
  '50th. Daniel דניאל. His attribute (the Sign of mercies), and according to others, the Angel of confessions (1). He corresponds to the holy name Pola, according to the language of the Samaritans. His ray begins from the 246th degree of the sphere up to the 145th, inclusively, corresponds to the 25th decade and to the genius named Eregbuo. He presides over the following days: 8 May, 19 July, 29 September, 10 December, 20 February. The invocation is made from 4 hours 20 minutes in the afternoon until 4 hours 40 minutes, reciting the 8th verse of psalm 102. (Miserator et misericors Dominus : longanimis et misericors.) He serves to obtain the mercy of God, and to have consolations. This genius governs justice, lawyers, attorneys, and all magistrates in general. He gives inspirations to those who are perplexed about several things, and do not know which they ought to decide upon. The person who is born under this influence will be industrious and active in business; they will love literature, and they will distinguish themselves by their eloquence.\n\nThe contrary genius influences swindlers, and all those who do not love work and seek to live by unlawful means...\n\n(1) Kircher, Œdipus Égyptiacus, volume 2, pages 266 and 267.',
  "51st. Hahasiah .ההשיה His attribute (Hidden God). He corresponds to the holy name of God Bila, according to the language of the Barsians. His ray begins from the 251st degree of the sphere up to the 255th, inclusively, corresponding to the 26th decade and to the genius named Sesmé, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following five days: 9 May, 20 July, 30 September, 11 December, 21 February. The invocation is made from 4 hours 40 minutes until 5 hours, pronouncing the 32nd verse of psalm 103. (Sit gloria Domini in sæculum : lætabitur Dominus in operibus suis.) He serves to elevate one's soul to the contemplation of divine things, and to discover the mysteries of wisdom. This genius rules over chemistry and physics; he reveals the greatest secrets of nature, notably the philosopher's stone and the universal medicine. The person who is born under this influence will love the abstract sciences; they will attach themselves particularly to knowing the properties and virtues attributed to animals, plants, and minerals; they will distinguish themselves in medicine by their marvellous cures, and they will make several discoveries useful to society.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over charlatans, and over all those who abuse the good faith of persons, by promising them extraordinary things.",
  "52nd. Imamiah עּממיׄה. His attribute (God elevated above all things). He corresponds to the name Abag, according to the language of the Melindese. His ray begins from the 256th degree of the sphere up to the 260th, inclusively, corresponding to the 26th decade and to the genius named Sagen. He presides over the five days following: 10 May, 21 July, 1 October, 12 December, 22 February. The invocation is made from 5 o'clock in the afternoon until 5 o'clock 20 minutes, reciting the 18th verse of psalm 7. (Confitebor Domino secundum justitiam ejus: et psallam nomini Domini altissimi.) He is good for destroying the power of enemies and for humbling them. This genius governs all journeys in general; he protects prisoners who have recourse to him, and inspires in them the means to obtain their liberty; he influences all those who seek the truth in good faith, and return from their errors by a truly sincere return to God. The person who is born under this influence will have a strong and vigorous temperament; they will bear adversities with much patience and courage; they will love work and will carry out with ease all that they wish.\n\nThe contrary genius governs pride, blasphemy, and wickedness; he influences coarse and quarrelsome men.",
  '53rd. Nanael. ננאׄאׄלּׄ. His attribute (God who abases the proud). He corresponds to the holy name Obra (1), according to the language of the Maltese. His ray begins from the 216th degree of the sphere up to the 265th, inclusively, corresponding to the 27th decade and to the genius named Chommé, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 11 May, 22 July, 2 October, 13 December, 23 February. The invocation is made from twenty minutes past five in the afternoon until forty minutes past five, pronouncing the divine names with the 75th verse of psalm 118. (Cognovi Domine quia æquitas judicia tua : et in veritate tua humiliasti me.) This psalm is divided into 22 equal parts, corresponding to the 22 Hebrew letters and to the 22 sacred names of God, which correspond to each of these letters, and which indicate the ladder by which the wise ascend to the contemplation of God. The cabalists claim that the holy Virgin recited it every day (see the Cabala of the Psalms). This genius rules over the high sciences; he influences clergymen, professors, magistrates, and men of law. The person who is born under this influence will have a melancholy temperament; they will love private life, rest and meditation; and they will distinguish themselves by their knowledge of the abstract sciences.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over ignorance and all the bad qualities of body and soul.\n\n(1) The holy name Obra corresponds to psalm 132, according to the cabala. This psalm teaches us that all men must love one another as brothers, that they must be united among themselves, and must all live together. It serves to obtain the friendship and favors of those one desires, and to live in peace with everyone.',
  "54th. Nithael ניׄתאׄלׄ His attribute (King of the heavens). He corresponds to the holy name Bora, according to the language of the Zaflanians. His ray begins from the 266th degree of the sphere up to the 270th, inclusively, corresponding to the 27th decade and to the genius named Chénon. He presides over the following five days: 12 May, 23 July, 3 October, 14 December, 24 February. The invocation is made from twenty minutes to six until six o'clock exactly in the afternoon, pronouncing the 19th verse of psalm 102 (Dominus in cœlo paravit sedem suam : et regnum ipsius omnibus dominabitur.) He serves to obtain the mercy of God and to live long. This genius rules over emperors, kings, princes, and all civil and ecclesiastical dignities. He watches over legitimate dynasties, and over the stability of empires; he gives a long and peaceful reign to princes who have recourse to him, and protects all those who wish to maintain themselves in their employments. The person who is born under this influence will become famous for their writings and their eloquence; they will have much reputation among the learned, will distinguish themselves by their virtues and will merit the confidence of their prince.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over the ruin of empires; he causes revolutions and upheavals; he influences all those who take part in the overthrow of monarchies in order to seize authority and the foremost employments.",
  "55th. Mebahiah מבהיה. Its attribute (Eternal God). It corresponds to the name Alay, according to the language of the peoples of Ormuz. Its ray begins from the 271st degree of the sphere up to the 275th, inclusively, corresponding to the 28th decade and to the genius named Smat, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the five days following: 13 May, 24 July, 4 October, 15 December, 25 February. The invocation is made from 6 o'clock in the afternoon until 20 minutes past 6; the request is pronounced with the divine names and the 13th verse of psalm 101. (Tu autem Domine in æternum permanes: et memoriale tuum in generationem). He is good for obtaining consolations, and for those who desire to have children. This genius governs morality and religion; he influences those who protect it with all their power, and spread it by every possible means. The person who is born under this influence will be distinguished by their good deeds, their piety, and by their zeal in fulfilling their duties toward God and men.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of truth; he influences all those who wish to destroy religion and the princes who protect it, so as to hinder the great work of the regeneration of mankind.",
  '56th. Poiel פוֹיאל. His attribute (God who sustains the universe). He corresponds to the holy name Illi, according to the language of the people of Aden. His ray begins from the 276th degree of the sphere up to the 280th, inclusively, corresponding to the 28th decade and to the genius named Themeso. He presides over the following days: 14 May, 25 July, 5 October, 16 December, 26 February. The invocation is made from 6 hours 20 minutes in the afternoon until 6 hours 40; one must pronounce the 15th verse of psalm 144. (Allevat Dominus omnes qui corruunt : et erigit omnes elisos.) He serves to obtain what one asks for. This genius governs fame, fortune, and philosophy. The person who is born under this influence will be esteemed by everyone for their modesty, their moderation, and their agreeable temper; they will owe their fortune only to their talents and to their conduct.\n\nThe contrary genius governs ambition and pride: it influences all those who set themselves up as masters and wish to raise themselves above others.',
  "57th. Nemamiah .נממיה Its attribute (God worthy of praise). He corresponds to the holy name Popa, according to the language of the Cyrenians. His ray begins from the 281st degree of the sphere up to the 285th, inclusively, corresponding to the 29th decade and to the genius named Srô, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the five days following: 15 May, 26 July, 6 October, 17 December, 27 February. This genius and those that follow, up to the 63rd, belong to the 8th order, which the orthodox call the choir of the archangels. The invocation is made from 6 hours 40 minutes in the afternoon until 7 o'clock, reciting the 19th verse of psalm 113. (Qui timent Dominum speraverunt in Domino : adjutor eorum et protector eorum est.) He serves to prosper in all things, and to deliver prisoners. This genius rules over great captains, admirals, generals, and all those who fight for a just cause. The person who is born under this influence will love the military profession; they will be distinguished by their activity, their bravery and their greatness of soul, and they will bear fatigues with much courage.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over betrayals, causes misunderstanding among leaders; it influences pusillanimous men, and those who attack defenceless persons.",
  "58th. Ieialel .יׄיׄלּׄאׄלּׄ Its attribute (God who hears the generations). He corresponds to the holy name Para, according to the language of the Celamites. His ray begins from the 286th degree of the sphere up to the 290th, inclusively, corresponding to the 29th decade and to the genius named Epima. He presides over the following five days: 16 May, 27 July, 7 October, 18 December, 28 February. The invocation is made from 7 o'clock in the afternoon until 20 minutes past 7.\n\nOne pronounces the divine names and the 3rd verse of psalm 6. (Et anima turbata est valde; sed tu Domine usque quo?) He serves against sorrows and cures illnesses, chiefly the ailment of the eyes (1). This genius governs iron; he influences armourers, locksmiths, cutlers, and all those who trade therein; he confounds the wicked and false witnesses. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves by their bravery and their frankness, and they will be passionate for Venus.\n\nThe contrary genius governs anger; he influences the wicked and murderers.\n\n(1) See on this subject the Enchiridion of Pope Leo, page 4.",
  '59th. Harahel. הרהאל His attribute (God who knows all things). He corresponds to the holy name of God Ella, according to the language of the Mesopotamians. His ray begins from the 291st degree of the sphere up to the 295th, inclusively, corresponding to the 30th decade and to the genius named Isrô, under the influence of the Sun. He presides over the following days: 17 May, 28 July, 8 October, 19 December, 1 March. The favourable hour begins from 7 hours 20 minutes until 7 hours 40; one must pronounce the name of the genius, with its attributes, and the 3rd verse of psalm 112 (A solis ortu usque ad occasum, laudabile nomen Domini.) It serves against the sterility of women, and to render children submissive and respectful toward their parents. This genius governs treasures, stockbrokers, public funds, archives, libraries, and all rare and precious collections; it has influence over printing, bookselling, and over all those who trade in them. The person who is born under this influence will love to instruct themselves in all the sciences in general; they will do much business, will follow the operations of the stock exchange, will speculate with advantage, and will distinguish themselves by their probity, their talents and their fortune.\n\nThe contrary genius is the enemy of learning; he causes ruin and destruction by fires; he has influence over squandering and fraudulent bankruptcies.',
  "60th. Mitzrael. מצראל His attribute (God who relieves the oppressed). He corresponds to the holy name Géna, according to the language of the peoples of Tibet. His ray begins from the 296th degree of the sphere up to the 300th, inclusively, corresponds to the 30th decade and to the genius named Homoth. He presides over the following days: 18 May, 29 July, 9 October; 20 December, 2 March. The invocation is made from twenty minutes to eight in the afternoon until eight o'clock, pronouncing the 18th verse of Psalm 144. (Justus Dominus in omnibus viis suis: et sanctus in omnibus operibus suis.) He serves to cure sicknesses of the mind, and to be delivered from those who persecute us; he rules over illustrious persons who distinguish themselves by their talents and their virtues; he influences the fidelity and obedience of subordinates toward their superiors. The person who is born under this influence will unite all the fine qualities of body and soul; they will be distinguished by their virtues, their wit, their agreeable temper, and they will live long.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over all insubordinate beings, and influences all bad physical and moral qualities.",
  "61st. Umabel .ומבאל His attribute (God above all things). He corresponds to the name Sila, according to the language of the ancient Bethulians. His ray begins from the 301st degree up to the 305th, inclusively, corresponding to the 31st decade and to the genius named Ptiau, under the influence of Venus. He presides over the following days: 19 May, 30 July, 10 October, 21 December, 3 March. The invocation must be made from eight o'clock in the afternoon until 8 hours 20 minutes; one pronounces the divine names and the 2nd verse of psalm 112. (Sit nomen Domini benedictum, ex hoc nunc et usque in sæculum.) He serves to obtain the friendship of a person. This genius governs astronomy and physics; he influences all those who distinguish themselves in that field. The person who is born under this influence will love travels, and all honest pleasures; they will have a sensitive heart, and love will cause them sorrows.\n\nThe contrary genius influences libertines, and particularly those who give themselves over to passions contrary to the order of nature.",
  '62nd. Iah-hel .יההאל His attribute (Supreme Being). He corresponds to the name Suna, according to the language of the ancient Carmanians. His ray begins from the 306th degree of the sphere up to the 301st, inclusively, corresponding to the 31st decade and to the genius named Oroasoer. He presides over the following days: 20 May, 31 July, 11 October, 22 December, 4 March. The invocation is made from 8 hours 20 minutes in the afternoon until 8 hours 40; one must pronounce the 159th verse of psalm 118. (Vide quoniam mandata tua dilexi Domine, in misericordiâ tuâ vivifica me.) He serves to acquire wisdom. This genius rules over philosophers, the enlightened, and all those who wish to withdraw from the world. The person who is born under this influence will love tranquility and solitude; they will exactly fulfill the duties of their station, and will distinguish themself by their modesty and virtues.\n\nThe contrary genius influences all that leads to scandal; he rules over luxury, inconstancy, and divorce; he provokes disunion between spouses.',
  "63rd. Anauel ענואל. His attribute is interpreted (God infinitely good). He corresponds to the holy name of the God Miri, according to the language of the Camboens. His ray begins from the 311th degree of the sphere up to the 315th, inclusively, corresponding to the 32nd decade and to the genius named Aseü, under the influence of Mercury. He presides over the following five days: the 21st of May, the 1st of August, the 12th of October, the 23rd of December, the 5th of March. The invocation is made from eight hours forty minutes in the afternoon until nine o'clock precisely, pronouncing the divine names and the 11th verse of Psalm 2. (Servite Domino in timore: et exultate ei cum tremore.) He serves to convert nations to Christianity, and to confound those who are its enemies. This genius protects against accidents; he preserves health and cures illnesses; he governs commerce, bankers, business agents and clerks. The person who is born under this influence will have a subtle and ingenious mind; they will distinguish themselves by their industry and their activity.\n\nThe contrary genius governs madness and prodigality; he influences all those who ruin themselves through their bad conduct.",
  "64th. Mehiel מהיאל. His attribute (God who gives life to all things). He corresponds to the holy name Alli, according to the language of the Mongols. His ray begins from the 316th degree of the sphere up to the 220th, inclusively, corresponding to the 32nd decade and to the genius named Astiro. He presides over the following days: 22 May, 2 August, 13 October, 24 December, 6 March. The invocation is made from 9 o'clock in the afternoon until 9 hours 20 minutes, pronouncing the divine names with the 18th verse of psalm 32. (Ecce oculi Domini super metuentes eum : et in eis, qui sperant super misericordiam ejus.) This psalm is good against adversities; it grants the prayers and wishes of those who hope in the mercy of God. This genius, and those that follow, up to the 72nd, belong to the 9th order, which the orthodox call the choir of angels. This genius protects against rabies and fierce animals; he governs scholars, professors, orators and authors; he has influence over printing and bookselling, and over all those who trade in them. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself in literature.\n\nThe contrary genius governs false scholars; he has influence over controversies, literary disputes and criticism.",
  '65th. Damabiah דמביה. Its attribute (God fountain of wisdom). He corresponds to the holy name Tara, according to the language of the Gymnosophists. His ray begins from the 321st degree of the sphere up to the 325th, inclusively, corresponding to the 33rd decade and to the genius named Ptébiou, under the influence of the Moon. He presides over the following days: 23 May, 3 August, 14 October, 25 December, 7 March. The invocation is made from 20 minutes past 9 in the afternoon until 40 minutes past 9, pronouncing the 15th verse of Psalm 89. (Convertere Domine, et usque qua? et deprecabilis esto super servos tuos.) It serves against sorceries, and to obtain wisdom and the success of useful undertakings. This genius governs the seas, rivers, springs, maritime expeditions, and naval construction; he influences sailors, pilots, fishing, and all those who trade in it. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself in the navy by their expeditions and discoveries and they will amass a considerable fortune.\n\nThe contrary genius causes storms and shipwrecks; it influences unfortunate expeditions.',
  "66th. Manakel מנקאה. His attribute (God who assists and maintains all things). He corresponds to the name Pora, according to the language of the Brahmins. His ray begins from the 326th degree of the sphere up to the 330th, inclusively, corresponding to the 33rd decade and to the genius named Tépisatras. He presides over the five days following: 24 May, 4 August, 15 October, 26 December, 8 March. The invocation is made from twenty minutes to ten in the afternoon until ten o'clock exactly, reciting the 22nd verse of psalm 37. (Ne derelinquas me Domine Deus meus; ne discesseris à me.) He serves to appease the anger of God, and to heal the falling sickness. He has dominion over vegetation and over aquatic animals; he has influence over sleep and over dreams. The person who is born under this influence will unite all the fine qualities of body and soul; they will win the friendship and goodwill of all good people by their amiability and the gentleness of their character.\n\nThe contrary genius has influence over all the bad physical and moral qualities.",
  "67th. Eïael אׄיעּאׄלּׄ. His attribute (God, delight of the children of men). He corresponds to the name Bogo, according to the language of the Albanians. His ray begins from the 331st degree up to the 335th, inclusively, corresponding to the 34th decade and to the genius named Abiou, under the influence of Saturn. He presides over the following days: 25 May, 5 August, 16 October, 27 December, 9 March. This genius is invoked from 10 o'clock in the evening until 10 o'clock 20 minutes; the request is pronounced with the divine names and the 4th verse of psalm 36. (Delectare in Domino et dabit tibi petitiones cordis tui.) It serves to have consolations in adversities, and to acquire wisdom. This genius governs changes, the preservation of monuments, and the longevity of life; he influences the occult sciences; he makes known the truth to those who have recourse to him in their labours. The person who is born under this influence will become illuminated by the spirit of God; they will love solitude, and they will distinguish themselves in the higher sciences, principally astronomy, physics, and philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs error, prejudices, and those who propagate erroneous systems.",
  '68th. Habuhiah הבויׄה. His attribute (God who gives with liberality.). He corresponds to the holy name Dépos, according to the language of the Peloponnesians. His ray begins from the 337th degree of the sphere up to the 340th, inclusively, corresponding to the 34th decade and to the genius named Archatapias. He presides over the following days: 26 May, 6 August, 17 October, 28 December, 10 March. The invocation is made from twenty past ten in the afternoon until ten forty, reciting the 1st verse of psalm 105. Confitemini Domino, quoniam bonus : quoniam in sæculum misericordia ejus.) He serves to preserve health and to cure diseases. This genius rules over agriculture and fecundity. The person who is born under this influence will love the countryside, hunting, gardens, and all that pertains to agriculture.\n\nThe contrary genius rules over sterility; it causes famine and plague; it influences the insects that harm the produce of the earth.',
  "69th. Rochel ראחאל. His attribute (God who sees all). He corresponds to the holy name Déos, according to the language of the Cretans. His ray begins from the 341st degree of the sphere up to the 345th, corresponding to the 35th decade and to the genius named Chontaré, under the influence of Jupiter. He presides over the following days: 27 May, 7 August, 18 October, 29 December, 11 March. The invocation is made from 10 hours 40 minutes in the afternoon until 11 o'clock exactly, pronouncing the 5th verse of psalm 15. (Dominus pars hæreditatis meæ, et calicis mei : tu es, qui restitues hæreditatem meam mihi.) He serves to recover lost or stolen objects, and to know the person who took them. This genius governs renown, fortune, and inheritances; he influences jurists, magistrates, solicitors, lawyers, and notaries. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themselves at the bar and in their knowledge of the customs, usages, and spirit of the laws of all peoples.\n\nThe contrary genius governs lawsuits, wills, and legacies made to the detriment of the rightful heirs; he influences all those who cause the ruin of families by provoking enormous costs and interminable lawsuits.",
  "70th. Jabamiah יׄבמיׄה (1). His attribute (Word which produces all things). He corresponds to the holy name Aris, according to the language of the Boeotians. His ray begins from the 346th degree of the sphere up to the 350th, inclusively, corresponding to the 35th decade and to the genius named Thopibui. He presides over the following five days: 28 May, 8 August, 19 October, 30 December, 12 March. The invocation is made every day from 11 o'clock in the evening until 11 o'clock 20 minutes. One must pronounce the request with the divine names and the 1st verse of Genesis: (In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth). This genius governs the generation of beings, and the phenomena of nature; he protects those who wish to regenerate themselves, and to re-establish in themselves the harmony that was broken by Adam's disobedience, which is achieved by exalting oneself toward God, and by purifying through the elements those things which compose the nature of man: it is then that the wise man re-enters the principle of creation; that he recovers his rights, his first dignity; that he becomes once more the master of nature, and that he enjoys all the prerogatives that God gave him in creating him. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself by their genius; they will be regarded by the learned of all nations, and they will become one of the foremost lights of philosophy.\n\nThe contrary genius governs atheism, and all those who propagate dangerous writings; he has influence over critics and literary disputes.\n\n(1) The Abbé de Villars says that this name expresses the eternal fecundity of God (see the Comte de Gabalis, 4th conversation). This work is found in the Recueil des voyages imaginaires et romans cabalistiques, volume 34. The author relates on this subject a singular story: \"When Noah wandered upon the avenging waves which flooded the universe, women were then reduced to a small number who saved themselves in the cabalistic ark that this second father of the world had built; this great man, groaning to see the dreadful punishment with which the Lord punished the crimes caused by the love that Adam had had for his Eve; seeing that Adam had lost his posterity by preferring Eve to the daughters of the elements; Noah, I say, having become wise by the disastrous example of Adam, consented that Vesta, his wife, should give herself to the salamander Oromasis, prince of the fiery substances, and persuaded his three children to also yield their three wives to the princes of the three other elements. The universe was in a short time repeopled with men so heroic, so learned, so admirable, that their posterity, dazzled by their virtues, took them for divinities. One of Noah's children, rebellious against his father's counsel, could not resist the attractions of his wife, any more than Adam could resist the charms of his Eve; but as Adam's sin had blackened all the souls of his descendants, the little indulgence that Ham had for the sylphs marked all his dark posterity; from this comes, our cabalists say, the horrible complexion of the Ethiopians, and of all those hideous peoples who are commanded to dwell beneath the torrid zone, in punishment for the profane ardor of their father. Noah came out of the Ark, and seeing that Vesta, his wife, only grew more beautiful through the commerce she had with her lover Oromasis, became passionate for her again. Ham, fearing that his father would go on to people the earth with children as black as his Ethiopians, seized his moment, one day when the good old man was full of wine, and castrated him without mercy. Oromasis, whom jealousy did not prevent from taking pity on the disgrace of his rival, taught his son Zoroaster, otherwise named Japhet, the name of the almighty God which expresses his eternal fecundity: Japhet pronounced six times, alternately with his brother Shem, walking backwards toward the patriarch, the fearsome name JABAMIAH; and they restored the old man to his entirety. This story, misunderstood, caused the Greeks to say that the oldest of the Gods had been castrated by one of his children.\"\n\nOne sees, in the Lettres cabalistiques, that the salvation of the cabalists was accomplished in Jabamiah and by Jabamiah.",
  "71st Haiaiel היׄיׄאׄלּׄ. Its attribute (God, master of the universe). It corresponds to the name Zeut, according to the language of the Phrygians. Its ray begins from the 351st degree of the sphere up to the 355th, inclusively, corresponding to the 36th decade and to the genius named Ptibiou, under the influence of Mars. He presides over the five days hereafter: 29 May, 9 August, 20 October, 31 December, 14 March. The invocation is made from 11 o'clock 20 minutes in the afternoon until 11 o'clock 40, pronouncing the 29th verse of psalm 108. (Confitebor Domino nimis in ore meo : et in medio multorum laudabo eum.) He serves to confound the wicked, and to deliver oneself from those who wish to oppress us. This genius protects all those who have recourse to him; he gives victory and peace, he influences iron, arsenals, fortified towns, and everything relating to military engineering. The person who is born under this influence will have much energy; they will love the military life, and will distinguish themselves by their bravery, talents and activity.\n\nThe contrary genius rules discord; he influences traitors, and all those who make themselves notorious by their crimes.",
  '72nd Mumiah. מומיה. His attribute is figured by the omega, which denotes the end of all things; he rules over Thrace or Roumelia. His ray begins from the 356th degree up to the 360th and last degree of the sphere, corresponding to the last decade and to the genius named Atembui. (See the sacred Calendar, page 41.) He presides over the following days: 30 May, 10 August, 21 October, 1 January, 14 March. The invocation is made from 11 hours 40 minutes in the afternoon until midnight precisely; one must pronounce the divine names, namely, alpha and omega, along with the name and attributes of the genius, as well as the request and the 7th verse of psalm 114. (Convertere anima mea in requiem tuam : quia Dominus benefecit tibi.) One must have a talisman which is on the frontispiece, with that of the genius written on the other side, which must be prepared under favourable influences indicated in the chapter on cabalistic Astrology. This genius protects in mysterious operations; he makes one succeed in all things, and brings every experiment to its end; he rules over chemistry, physics and medicine, he influences the health and longevity of life. The person who is born under this influence will distinguish themself in medicine; they will make themself celebrated by their marvellous cures, will unveil several secrets of nature which will make the happiness of the children of the earth, and they will devote their vigils and their cares to relieving the poor and the sick.\n\nThe contrary genius causes despair and suicide; he influences all those who detest their existence and the day that saw them born.\n\nI have indicated, in the preceding chapters, the manner of knowing the genii who influence the universe, nature and man; it follows from all that I have said, that the genii each rule ten days of the year. One sees first by the second table, page 28, that the first genius rules from the 20th of March until the 24th, inclusively, which make five days, and by the third table, page 32, this first genius rules again five other days, by the effect of the five revolutions which take place every 72 days, for from the 20th of March until the 30th of May, there are 72 days, and the 31st of May which is the 73rd, corresponds to the first genius, and so on.',
]
